<main><section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>Research discipline, applied to practical data and software systems.</h1><p class="section-lead">I use analysis, machine learning and engineering to solve real-world problems where technical work needs to produce an understandable and defensible practical result.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="container content">
<h2>How I work</h2>
<p>I start with the real decision or operational problem, then ask what data would actually be available, what could go wrong, how the result should be validated and what a non-technical stakeholder ultimately needs to know.</p>
<div class="callout">The standard I aim for is simple: a result should be credible enough to defend, useful enough to act on, and clear enough to explain.</div>
<h2>What I work on</h2>
<ul>
<li>Applied machine learning, classification, regression and ranking</li>
<li>NLP, semantic modelling and published stance-classification research</li>
<li>Data engineering, warehousing, CDC and analytical data platforms</li>
<li>Backend/API engineering, persistence, idempotency and third-party integrations</li>
<li>Time-series modelling and predictive-maintenance research</li>
<li>Computer vision, currently through the in-progress MonReader classifier</li>
<li>Frontend/product development, currently through the in-progress Reel Good application</li>
<li>Model validation, leakage control, reliability and evidence-driven interpretation</li>
</ul>
<h2>How to read the portfolio</h2>
<p>The seven completed case studies are presented as evidence-backed work. Reel Good and MonReader are shown separately as projects in progress so their current direction is visible without implying that unfinished work is complete.</p>
<p><a class="cta" href="/case-studies">View case studies</a></p>
